  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advanced Document Examination Training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project Advanced Document Examination Training seeks to address the challenges posed by irregular migration and transnational organized crime (TOC), i.e. trafficking in persons and migrant smuggling, through enhanced capacities to detect document and identity frauds. While capacities are built through the training programme, the network of involved experts across selected Mekong countries would also be strengthened, hereby contributing to future regional law enforcement information sharing, which is a key element of the fight against TOC. The project prioritizes activities that will develop the capacities of law enforcement agencies and border officials to counter irregular migration and TOC by providing them with necessary skills and tools to enhance their ability to detect and counter document and identity fraud, ensuring effective border control measures and protecting genuine legal identities.</narrative>
  </description>
